'''Batwing''' is an [[Ancient Weapons|ancient]] knife that was originally obtainable by purchasing the [[Batwing Gamepass]] for 2,499 Robux during the [[Halloween Event 2018|2018 Halloween Event]]. It is now only obtainable through trading as the [[Gamepasses|gamepass]] has since went offsale.

==Appearance==
It has a relatively long thin black handle with a small curved grip on the bottom with finger nubs engraved on it. Attached to the top of the handle is the blade’s ring clamp that looks like a bat with a red crystal on top of its head. The actual blades of the scythe are made out of the red and black wings of the bat, hence the name.

==Trivia==
* It has a teal variant under the name [[Nik's Scythe]], that can only be obtained as a gift from [[Nikilis]].
*Batwing was originally a [[Nikilis]] exclusive item. This is also the reason why [[Nik's Scythe]] is a Batwing reskin.
*Its model derives from the Roblox gear [https://www.roblox.com/catalog/306971294/Bat-Scythe Bat Scythe], purchasable from the avatar shop for 500 Robux.
*Its model, published by [[Nikilis]], can be found [http://www.roblox.com/Scythe-item?id=375690925 here].
*It was mass duped upon its release, causing [[Nikilis]] to reskin all the duped Batwings to the [[Common Weapons|common]] knife [[Glitch1]]. In fact, it was the main victim of [[The Batwing Glitch (2018)]].
*It was a heavily targeted victim of the [[The Duping Glitch (2021)|Duping Glitch (2021)]] and the [[The Duping Glitch (2022)|Duping Glitch (2022)]].
* This was the first [[Ancient Weapons|ancient]] shop item to be released in [[Murder Mystery 2]].
* This was the first [[Ancient Weapons|ancient]] to be released into the game and stay as one.
** [[Flames]] does not count as it was changed to Godly.
*It is commonly partnered with the [[Godly Weapons|godly]] gun [[Darkbringer]] however, it is not considered a <u>set</u>.
*This is one of the few scythes in game, the others being [[Nik's Scythe]], [[Icewing]], [[Elderwood Scythe]], [[Hallowscythe]], [[Reaver]] and [[Gingerscythe|Gingerscythe.]]

